8
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:21.870
Cal has been holding this family together for seven years.

9
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.870
Every dime he spent came from his own savings.

10
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.370
He came into this family with absolutely nothing.

11
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.870
The least he could do is contribute some money and effort to this house.

12
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:30.870
Enough!

13
00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.870
Is your mother supposed to track every single payment?

14
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:33.870
He chose to stay home.

15
00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.870
Now he's blaming us for his own choices?

16
00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:37.870
Exactly. It's just five grand a month.

17
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:38.870
You give this family everything.

18
00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.370
What right does he have to complain?

19
00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.870
What right does he have to ask for a divorce?

20
00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:42.870
Just five grand.

21
00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:45.870
Cal is so damn petty, but he took it way too far this time.

22
00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.870
You think someone is putting him up to this?

23
00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:49.870
He's suddenly so dead set on a divorce.

24
00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.870
You think he's seen another woman?

25
00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.870
Yes! He has to be!

26
00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.870
Why else would he just suddenly demand a divorce?

27
00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:03.120
He's cooking.

28
00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:08.960
Forget it. Let's not talk about this right now.

29
00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.960
Mom, can you just make Willa something to eat?

30
00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.960
Grandma, I want spaghetti with lots of cheese.

31
00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.960
